v class="mt-3 flex flex-wrap items-center gap-3"><img alt="MIT logo" loading="lazy" width="400" height="400" decoding="async" data-nimg="1" class="artwork-surface dark:p-1 w-10" style="color:transparent" srcSet="/_next/image?url=%2Fmit.png&amp;w=640&amp;q=75 1x, /_next/image?url=%2Fmit.png&amp;w=828&amp;q=75 2x" src="/_next/image?url=%2Fmit.png&amp;w=828&amp;q=75"/><span class="text-sm text-brand-neutral-400">/</span><span class="text-sm text-primary-700 dark:text-primary-200">To appear in NeurIPS 2026</span></div></div><div class="flex flex-row items-center gap-8  "><div class="flex flex-row items-center gap-8"><a href="https://github.com/sophicle/sensory" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" class="group block rounded-sm outline-none focus-visible:ring-2 focus-visible:ring-brand-neutral-500/30 focus-visible:ring-offset-2 focus-visible:ring-offset-white dark:focus-visible:ring-brand-neutral-300/30 dark:focus-visible:ring-offset-brand-neutral-950"><div class="flex flex-col items-center"><p class="text-brand-neutral-950 underline decoration-dotted decoration-1 underline-offset-[3px] transition-colors group-hover:text-teal-600 group-focus-visible:text-teal-600 dark:text-brand-neutral-50 dark:group-hover:text-teal-300 dark:group-focus-visible:text-teal-300 font-mono text-sm">[<!-- -->Code<!-- -->]</p><img alt="GitHub thumbnail" loading="lazy" width="1200" height="0" decoding="async" data-nimg="1" class="mt-2 pointer transition-transform duration-300 ease-in-out hover:scale-[1.015] w-42" style="color:transparent" sizes="168px" srcSet="/_next/image?url=%2Fsensory%2Fgithubthumb_opt.webp&amp;w=16&amp;q=75 16w, /_next/image?url=%2Fsensory%2Fgithubthumb_opt.webp&amp;w=32&amp;q=75 32w, /_next/image?url=%2Fsensory%2Fgithubthumb_opt.webp&amp;w=48&amp;q=75 48w, /_next/image?url=%2Fsensory%2Fgithubthumb_opt.webp&amp;w=64&amp;q=75 64w, /_next/image?url=%2Fsensory%2Fgithubthumb_opt.webp&amp;w=96&amp;q=75 96w, /_next/image?url=%2Fsensory%2Fgithubthumb_opt.webp&amp;w=128&amp;q=75 128w, /_next/image?url=%2Fsensory%2Fgithubthumb_opt.webp&amp;w=256&amp;q=75 256w, /_next/image?url=%2Fsensory%2Fgithubthumb_opt.webp&amp;w=384&amp;q=75 384w, /_next/image?url=%2Fsensory%2Fgithubthumb_opt.webp&amp;w=640&amp;q=75 640w, /_next/image?url=%2Fsensory%2Fgithubthumb_opt.webp&amp;w=750&amp;q=75 750w, /_next/image?url=%2Fsensory%2Fgithubthumb_opt.webp&amp;w=828&amp;q=75 828w, /_next/image?url=%2Fsensory%2Fgithubthumb_opt.webp&amp;w=1080&amp;q=75 1080w, /_next/image?url=%2Fsensory%2Fgithubthumb_opt.webp&amp;w=1200&amp;q=75 1200w, /_next/image?url=%2Fsensory%2Fgithubthumb_opt.webp&amp;w=1920&amp;q=75 1920w, /_next/image?url=%2Fsensory%2Fgithubthumb_opt.webp&amp;w=2048&amp;q=75 2048w, /_next/image?url=%2Fsensory%2Fgithubthumb_opt.webp&amp;w=3840&amp;q=75 3840w" src="/_next/image?url=%2Fsensory%2Fgithubthumb_opt.webp&amp;w=3840&amp;q=75"/></div></a><a href="https://arxiv.org/abs/2510.02425" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" class="group block rounded-sm outline-none focus-visible:ring-2 focus-visible:ring-brand-neutral-500/30 focus-visible:ring-offset-2 focus-visible:ring-offset-white dark:focus-visible:ring-brand-neutral-300/30 dark:focus-visible:ring-offset-brand-neutral-950"><div class="flex flex-col items-center"><p class="text-brand-neutral-950 underline decoration-dotted decoration-1 underline-offset-[3px] transition-colors group-hover:text-teal-600 group-focus-visible:text-teal-600 dark:text-brand-neutral-50 dark:group-hover:text-teal-300 dark:group-focus-visible:text-teal-300 font-mono text-sm">[<!-- -->Paper<!-- -->]</p><img alt="Paper thumbnail" loading="lazy" width="1200" height="0" decoding="async" data-nimg="1" class="mt-2 pointer transition-transform duration-300 ease-in-out hover:scale-[1.015] h-28 w-auto shadow-[0_0_1px_1px_rgba(0,0,0,0.35),5px_5px_0_0_#fff,5px_5px_1px_1px_rgba(0,0,0,0.35),10px_10px_0_0_#fff,10px_10px_1px_1px_rgba(0,0,0,0.35)]" style="color:transparent" sizes="112px" srcSet="/_next/image?url=%2Fsensory%2Fpaperthumb_opt.webp&amp;w=16&amp;q=75 16w, /_next/image?url=%2Fsensory%2Fpaperthumb_opt.webp&amp;w=32&amp;q=75 32w, /_next/image?url=%2Fsensory%2Fpaperthumb_opt.webp&amp;w=48&amp;q=75 48w, /_next/image?url=%2Fsensory%2Fpaperthumb_opt.webp&amp;w=64&amp;q=75 64w, /_next/image?url=%2Fsensory%2Fpaperthumb_opt.webp&amp;w=96&amp;q=75 96w, /_next/image?url=%2Fsensory%2Fpaperthumb_opt.webp&amp;w=128&amp;q=75 128w, /_next/image?url=%2Fsensory%2Fpaperthumb_opt.webp&amp;w=256&amp;q=75 256w, /_next/image?url=%2Fsensory%2Fpaperthumb_opt.webp&amp;w=384&amp;q=75 384w, /_next/image?url=%2Fsensory%2Fpaperthumb_opt.webp&amp;w=640&amp;q=75 640w, /_next/image?url=%2Fsensory%2Fpaperthumb_opt.webp&amp;w=750&amp;q=75 750w, /_next/image?url=%2Fsensory%2Fpaperthumb_opt.webp&amp;w=828&amp;q=75 828w, /_next/image?url=%2Fsensory%2Fpaperthumb_opt.webp&amp;w=1080&amp;q=75 1080w, /_next/image?url=%2Fsensory%2Fpaperthumb_opt.webp&amp;w=1200&amp;q=75 1200w, /_next/image?url=%2Fsensory%2Fpaperthumb_opt.webp&amp;w=1920&amp;q=75 1920w, /_next/image?url=%2Fsensory%2Fpaperthumb_opt.webp&amp;w=2048&amp;q=75 2048w, /_next/image?url=%2Fsensory%2Fpaperthumb_opt.webp&amp;w=3840&amp;q=75 3840w" src="/_next/image?url=%2Fsensory%2Fpaperthumb_opt.webp&amp;w=3840&amp;q=75"/></div></a></div></div></header><div class="relative w-full max-w-3xl mx-auto" style="perspective:1000px"><div class="relative w-full aspect-[16/9] transition-transform duration-700 transform-style-preserve-3d" style="transform:rotateY(0deg)"><div class="absolute w-full h-full backface-hidden flex items-center justify-center hover:scale-[1.015] transition-transform duration-300 ease-in-out pointer" style="backface-visibility:hidden"><img alt="Plato Prompt Diagram" loading="lazy" decoding="async" data-nimg="fill" class="pointer-events-none artwork-surface bg-white p-3 object-contain" style="position:absolute;height:100%;width:100%;left:0;top:0;right:0;bottom:0;color:transparent" sizes="(max-width: 1024px) 100vw, 768px" srcSet="/_next/image?url=%2Fsensory%2Fplato_prompt_diagram_opt.webp&amp;w=640&amp;q=75 640w, /_next/image?url=%2Fsensory%2Fplato_prompt_diagram_opt.webp&amp;w=750&amp;q=75 750w, /_next/image?url=%2Fsensory%2Fplato_prompt_diagram_opt.webp&amp;w=828&amp;q=75 828w, /_next/image?url=%2Fsensory%2Fplato_prompt_diagram_opt.webp&amp;w=1080&amp;q=75 1080w, /_next/image?url=%2Fsensory%2Fplato_prompt_diagram_opt.webp&amp;w=1200&amp;q=75 1200w, /_next/image?url=%2Fsensory%2Fplato_prompt_diagram_opt.webp&amp;w=1920&amp;q=75 1920w, /_next/image?url=%2Fsensory%2Fplato_prompt_diagram_opt.webp&amp;w=2048&amp;q=75 2048w, /_next/image?url=%2Fsensory%2Fplato_prompt_diagram_opt.webp&amp;w=3840&amp;q=75 3840w" src="/_next/image?url=%2Fsensory%2Fplato_prompt_diagram_opt.webp&amp;w=3840&amp;q=75"/></div><div class="absolute w-full h-full backface-hidden" style="transform:rotateY(180deg);backface-visibility:hidden"><div class="w-full h-full bg-white"></div><button class="group inline-flex items-start gap-1 mt-2 opacity-60 hover:opacity-100 transition-opacity self-center"><svg width="15" height="15" viewBox="0 0 15 15" fill="none" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" class="w-3 h-3 transition-transform duration-200 group-hover:-translate-x-1"><path d="M6.85355 3.14645C7.04882 3.34171 7.04882 3.65829 6.85355 3.85355L3.70711 7H12.5C12.7761 7 13 7.22386 13 7.5C13 7.77614 12.7761 8 12.5 8H3.70711L6.85355 11.1464C7.04882 11.3417 7.04882 11.6583 6.85355 11.8536C6.65829 12.0488 6.34171 12.0488 6.14645 11.8536L2.14645 7.85355C1.95118 7.65829 1.95118 7.34171 2.14645 7.14645L6.14645 3.14645C6.34171 2.95118 6.65829 2.95118 6.85355 3.14645Z" fill="currentColor" fill-rule="evenodd" clip-rule="evenodd"></path></svg><span class="text-xs">return</span></button></div></div></div><div class="text-base leading-relaxed flex flex-col space-y-4"><p class="">Language models are trained to predict the next word—not to see or hear. But what happens to the model&#x27;s representation when we ask it to imagine what its inputs look or sound like? We find that:</p><div class="w-full"><div class="p-3 w-full lg:w-5/6 mx-auto rounded-none border border-brand-neutral-200 dark:border-brand-neutral-600 text-center bg-white dark:bg-brand-neutral-700"><span class="block text-sm font-mono">A simple cue like asking the model to &#x27;see&#x27; or &#x27;hear&#x27; can push a purely text-trained language model towards the representations of purely image-trained or purely-audio trained encoders.</span></div></div><p class="">This effect arises without the language model ever receiving actual visual or auditory input. Our result is unlike the &#x27;tikz unicorn&#x27; effect, where language models produce plausible text that mimics sensory descriptions.</p><h2 class="Typography_heading__ut9qe Typography_h2__K9xvD PaperEditorial_heading__0PQ9z">What representations are we using?</h2><div class="grid grid-cols-1 md:grid-cols-2 gap-4 items-start "><div class="text-leftleading-relaxed flex flex-col space-y-4 "><p>A representation can be characterized by its<!-- --> <span class="italic">kernel</span>, described by the pairwise similarities among the vectors a neural network yields over a set of inputs. Measures of representation similarity quantify how closely the geometry of two such kernels align. The specific measure that we use is called mutual<!-- --> <span class="italic">k</span>-nearest neighbors (mutual-<span class="italic">k</span>NN).</p><p>Cross-modal convergence has recently been observed as models scale<a href="#reference-1" aria-label="Reference 1" class="whitespace-nowrap tabular-nums">[<!-- -->1<!-- -->]</a>. However, prior work treats representations, and thus alignment, as fixed properties of models. That is, alignment is currently understood to emerge passively. In our work, we demonstrate that we can<!-- --> <span class="italic">steer</span> representations at inference time. When a language model is asked to generate, each output token involves another forward pass through the network; averaging the activations across time steps yields a<!-- --> <span class="italic">generative representation</span>.</p></div><div class="relative w-full max-w-3xl mx-auto" style="perspective:1000px"><div class="relative w-full aspect-[16/9] transition-transform duration-700 transform-style-preserve-3d" style="transform:rotateY(0deg)"><div class="absolute w-full h-full backface-hidden flex items-center justify-center hover:scale-[1.015] transition-transform duration-300 ease-in-out pointer" style="backface-visibility:hidden"><img alt="Generative Representations" loading="lazy" decoding="async" data-nimg="fill" class="pointer-events-none artwork-surface bg-white p-3 object-contain" style="position:absolute;height:100%;width:100%;left:0;top:0;right:0;bottom:0;color:transparent" sizes="(max-width: 1024px) 100vw, 768px" srcSet="/_next/image?url=%2Fsensory%2Fgenerative_opt.webp&amp;w=640&amp;q=75 640w, /_next/image?url=%2Fsensory%2Fgenerative_opt.webp&amp;w=750&amp;q=75 750w, /_next/image?url=%2Fsensory%2Fgenerative_opt.webp&amp;w=828&amp;q=75 828w, /_next/image?url=%2Fsensory%2Fgenerative_opt.webp&amp;w=1080&amp;q=75 1080w, /_next/image?url=%2Fsensory%2Fgenerative_opt.webp&amp;w=1200&amp;q=75 1200w, /_next/image?url=%2Fsensory%2Fgenerative_opt.webp&amp;w=1920&amp;q=75 1920w, /_next/image?url=%2Fsensory%2Fgenerative_opt.webp&amp;w=2048&amp;q=75 2048w, /_next/image?url=%2Fsensory%2Fgenerative_opt.webp&amp;w=3840&amp;q=75 3840w" src="/_next/image?url=%2Fsensory%2Fgenerative_opt.webp&amp;w=3840&amp;q=75"/></div><div class="absolute w-full h-full backface-hidden" style="transform:rotateY(180deg);backface-visibility:hidden"><div class="w-full h-full bg-white"></div><button class="group inline-flex items-start gap-1 mt-2 opacity-60 hover:opacity-100 transition-opacity self-center"><svg width="15" height="15" viewBox="0 0 15 15" fill="none" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" class="w-3 h-3 transition-transform duration-200 group-hover:-translate-x-1"><path d="M6.85355 3.14645C7.04882 3.34171 7.04882 3.65829 6.85355 3.85355L3.70711 7H12.5C12.7761 7 13 7.22386 13 7.5C13 7.77614 12.7761 8 12.5 8H3.70711L6.85355 11.1464C7.04882 11.3417 7.04882 11.6583 6.85355 11.8536C6.65829 12.0488 6.34171 12.0488 6.14645 11.8536L2.14645 7.85355C1.95118 7.65829 1.95118 7.34171 2.14645 7.14645L6.14645 3.14645C6.34171 2.95118 6.65829 2.95118 6.85355 3.14645Z" fill="currentColor" fill-rule="evenodd" clip-rule="evenodd"></path></svg><span class="text-xs">return</span></button></div></div></div></div><div class="text-base leading-relaxed flex flex-col space-y-4"><h2 class="Typography_heading__ut9qe Typography_h2__K9xvD PaperEditorial_heading__0PQ9z">Samples of generated outputs</h2><p>So, what happens to alignment when we ask the language model to imagine other modalities? Here are samples of what output tokens look like with and without sensory cues. These examples show how explicitly asking the model to &#x27;see&#x27; or &#x27;hear&#x27; encourages the language model to articulate a scene as if through that sense.</p><p class="text-sm italic text-brand-neutral-600 dark:text-brand-neutral-300">Note: We highlight, by hand, words that may be associated with the sensory modality.</p></div></div><section class="flex flex-col items-center"><div class="w-full max-w-5xl flex items-center justify-between gap-4"><div class="flex-1  px-2"><div class="Cues_figureTypography__QTQmK FigureTokens_tokens__PlltK mb-4"><div class="Cues_problemControls__tK1VL"><button type="button" aria-label="Previous example" class=""><svg width="15" height="15" viewBox="0 0 15 15" fill="none" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M8.84182 3.13514C9.04327 3.32401 9.05348 3.64042 8.86462 3.84188L5.43521 7.49991L8.86462 11.1579C9.05348 11.3594 9.04327 11.6758 8.84182 11.8647C8.64036 12.0535 8.32394 12.0433 8.13508 11.8419L4.38508 7.84188C4.20477 7.64955 4.20477 7.35027 4.38508 7.15794L8.13508 3.15794C8.32394 2.95648 8.64036 2.94628 8.84182 3.13514Z" fill="currentColor" fill-rule="evenodd" clip-rule="evenodd"></path></svg></button><span>Example<!-- --> <!-- -->1<!-- --> of <!-- -->6</span><button type="button" aria-label="Next example" class=""><svg width="15" height="15" viewBox="0 0 15 15" fill="none" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M6.1584 3.13508C6.35985 2.94621 6.67627 2.95642 6.86514 3.15788L10.6151 7.15788C10.7954 7.3502 10.7954 7.64949 10.6151 7.84182L6.86514 11.8418C6.67627 12.0433 6.35985 12.0535 6.1584 11.8646C5.95694 11.6757 5.94673 11.3593 6.1356 11.1579L9.565 7.49985L6.1356 3.84182C5.94673 3.64036 5.95694 3.32394 6.1584 3.13508Z" fill="currentColor" fill-rule="evenodd" clip-rule="evenodd"></path></svg></button><span class="Cues_srOnly__0ycwe" aria-live="polite"></span></div></div><div class="flex flex-col md:flex-row items-start gap-6"><div class="md:w-1/3 w-full flex flex-col items-center flex-shrink-0"><a href="/sensory/sample_239.png" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer"><img alt="Sample 1" loading="lazy" width="300" height="300" decoding="async" data-nimg="1" class="max-h-84 object-cover mb-2 transform rotate-[-1.5deg] hover:rotate-0 hover:scale-[1.015] transition-transform duration-300  ease-in-out " style="color:transparent" srcSet="/_next/image?url=%2Fsensory%2Fsample_239.webp&amp;w=384&amp;q=75 1x, /_next/image?url=%2Fsensory%2Fsample_239.webp&amp;w=640&amp;q=75 2x" src="/_next/image?url=%2Fsensory%2Fsample_239.webp&amp;w=640&amp;q=75"/></a><div class="mt-4"><p class="text-xl italic">&quot;<!-- -->Awaiting a pitch — batter, catcher, and umpire in baseball<!-- -->&quot;</p><p class="text-sm text-brand-neutral-600 dark:text-brand-neutral-300 mt-1">Source: Wikipedia-based Image–Text Dataset<a href="#reference-2" aria-label="Reference 2" class="whitespace-nowrap tabular-nums">[<!-- -->2<!-- -->]</a></p></div></div><div class="md:flex-1 w-full flex flex-col  justify-center "><div class="font-mono mb-3 text-sm border border-brand-neutral-200 dark:border-brand-neutral-600 bg-white dark:bg-brand-neutral-800 rounded-none px-4 py-2 mx-auto text-center inline-block">Imagine what it would look like to see: <!-- -->{caption}</div><div class="w-full"><div class="flex gap-2 w-max text-sm font-mono [&amp;_*]:font-mono"><button type="button" class="px-4 py-1 pointer rounded-none border border-b-0 border-brand-neutral-200 dark:border-brand-neutral-600 bg-white dark:bg-brand-neutral-800 text-brand-neutral-900 dark:text-white !font-mono" aria-pressed="true"><span class="text-blue-400">SEE</span><span> cue</span></button><button type="button" class="px-4 py-1 pointer rounded-none border border-b-0 border-brand-neutral-200 dark:border-brand-neutral-600 bg-brand-neutral-100 dark:bg-brand-neutral-700 text-brand-neutral-600 dark:text-brand-neutral-200 !font-mono" aria-pressed="false"><span class="text-red-400">HEAR</span><span> cue</span></button><button type="button" class="px-4 py-1 pointer rounded-none border border-b-0 border-brand-neutral-200 dark:border-brand-neutral-600 bg-brand-neutral-100 dark:bg-brand-neutral-700 text-brand-neutral-600 dark:text-brand-neutral-200 !font-mono" aria-pressed="false"><span>No cue</span></button></div><div class="border border-brand-neutral-200 dark:border-brand-neutral-600 bg-white dark:bg-brand-neutral-800 rounded-none px-4 py-3"><code class="block text-sm font-mono leading-relaxed whitespace-pre-wrap max-h-64 overflow-auto">...I need to<!-- --> <span class="text-blue-400 font-medium font-mono">visualize</span> <!-- -->a baseball field. The batter stands at the home plate, right? They&#x27;re<!-- --> <span class="text-blue-400 font-medium font-mono">holding the bat</span>, probably in a ready position, feet shoulder-width apart. Their<!-- --> <span class="text-blue-400 font-medium font-mono">body language</span> <!-- -->should show they’re focused, maybe squinting at the catcher or the umpire...</code></div></div></div></div></div></div></section><section class=""><h2 class="Typography_heading__ut9qe Typography_h2__K9xvD PaperEditorial_heading__0PQ9z">Sensory cues steer generative representations</h2><div class="grid grid-cols-1 md:grid-cols-2 gap-4 items-start "><div class="text-leftleading-relaxed flex flex-col space-y-4 "><p>While it is expected that the output follow the prompt, what&#x27;s interesting is that the generative representations produced over these tokens become increasingly similar to those of the modality that match the given sensory cue. That is, a<!-- --> <span class="text-blue-400 font-mono">SEE</span> cue ( or<!-- --> <span class="text-red-400 font-mono">HEAR</span> cue) increases alignment to the vision (or audio) encoder relative to the no cue baseline. See the star in the figure, which denotes matching cue-modality.</p><p>We find that this effect is specific to generative representations: appending a sensory prompt to the caption does not increase alignment for single-pass embedding representations, and in fact reduced it. Thus, the elicited higher alignment is a result of the representation formed through generation.</p></div><figure class="flex flex-col items-center"><img alt="Sensory Prompting Alignment Trend" loading="lazy" width="800" height="400" decoding="async" data-nimg="1" class="w-full bg-white p-3" style="color:transparent" sizes="(max-width: 768px) 100vw, 50vw" srcSet="/_next/image?url=%2Fsensory%2Fsensory_prompting_trend_embed_vs_generate_opt.webp&amp;w=384&amp;q=75 384w, /_next/image?url=%2Fsensory%2Fsensory_prompting_trend_embed_vs_generate_opt.webp&amp;w=640&amp;q=75 640w, /_next/image?url=%2Fsensory%2Fsensory_prompting_trend_embed_vs_generate_opt.webp&amp;w=750&amp;q=75 750w, /_next/image?url=%2Fsensory%2Fsensory_prompting_trend_embed_vs_generate_opt.webp&amp;w=828&amp;q=75 828w, /_next/image?url=%2Fsensory%2Fsensory_prompting_trend_embed_vs_generate_opt.webp&amp;w=1080&amp;q=75 1080w, /_next/image?url=%2Fsensory%2Fsensory_prompting_trend_embed_vs_generate_opt.webp&amp;w=1200&amp;q=75 1200w, /_next/image?url=%2Fsensory%2Fsensory_prompting_trend_embed_vs_generate_opt.webp&amp;w=1920&amp;q=75 1920w, /_next/image?url=%2Fsensory%2Fsensory_prompting_trend_embed_vs_generate_opt.webp&amp;w=2048&amp;q=75 2048w, /_next/image?url=%2Fsensory%2Fsensory_prompting_trend_embed_vs_generate_opt.webp&amp;w=3840&amp;q=75 3840w" src="/_next/image?url=%2Fsensory%2Fsensory_prompting_trend_embed_vs_generate_opt.webp&amp;w=3840&amp;q=75"/><figcaption class="text-sm text-brand-neutral-600 dark:text-brand-neutral-300 mt-2">Sensory cued alignment using single-pass embedding and generative representations. Error bars denote ±1 bootstrap standard error, computed over rows of the mutual-<span class="italic">k</span>NN kernel.</figcaption></figure></div></section><section class=""><h2 class="Typography_heading__ut9qe Typography_h2__K9xvD PaperEditorial_heading__0PQ9z">Visualization of mutual-<span class="italic">k</span>NN</h2><div class="text-base leading-relaxed flex flex-col space-y-4 mb-4"><p class="">Mutual-<span class="italic">k</span>NN is interpretable as a measure of kernel similarity. Below, we display image-caption pairs from the Wikipedia-based Image-Text dataset<a href="#reference-2" aria-label="Reference 2" class="whitespace-nowrap tabular-nums">[<!-- -->2<!-- -->]</a>. We visualize <span class="italic">k</span> <!-- -->nearest neighbors in the vision encoder and language model (under no cue and a visual cue). Samples are ordered by the change in mutual-<span class="italic">k</span>NN overlap between the language model and the vision encoder, so that examples where the<!-- --> <span class="text-blue-400 font-mono">SEE</span> cue yields the largest relative increase appear first. Blue outlines indicate that the neighbor is also a neighbor in the vision encoder</p></div><div class="Cues_figureTypography__QTQmK FigureTokens_tokens__PlltK"><div class="flex flex-col gap-4 h-[850px]"><div class="flex flex-wrap gap-2 items-center justify-between w-full"><input type="text" aria-label="Search by caption or index" placeholder="Search by caption or index..." class="px-2 py-1 border border-black w-64 max-w-full text-xs bg-white" value=""/><div class="flex items-center gap-2"><label for="sensory-neighbors" class="text-xs text-brand-neutral-600 dark:text-brand-neutral-300">Neighbors (k):</label><input id="sensory-neighbors" type="range" min="5" max="10" step="1" class="w-16 accent-blue-400" value="10"/><span class="text-xs font-mono">10</span></div><button type="button" aria-expanded="false" class="bevel-button px-2 py-1 text-xs">Show generations</button><select aria-label="Sort sensory examples" class="min-w-0 max-w-full px-2 py-1 border border-black text-xs bg-white"><option value="overlapDesc" selected="">Visual cue yields largest relative increase first</option><option value="overlapAsc">Visual cue yields largest relative increase last</option><option value="id">Sort by ID</option></select></div><div class="flex-1 overflow-y-auto pr-2"><div class="flex flex-col gap-8"></div></div></div><div class="Cues_problemControls__tK1VL"><button type="button" disabled="" class="disabled:opacity-40" aria-label="Previous"><svg width="15" height="15" viewBox="0 0 15 15" fill="none" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" class="w-5 h-5 text-brand-neutral-500 dark:text-brand-neutral-300"><path d="M8.84182 3.13514C9.04327 3.32401 9.05348 3.64042 8.86462 3.84188L5.43521 7.49991L8.86462 11.1579C9.05348 11.3594 9.04327 11.6758 8.84182 11.8647C8.64036 12.0535 8.32394 12.0433 8.13508 11.8419L4.38508 7.84188C4.20477 7.64955 4.20477 7.35027 4.38508 7.15794L8.13508 3.15794C8.32394 2.95648 8.64036 2.94628 8.84182 3.13514Z" fill="currentColor" fill-rule="evenodd" clip-rule="evenodd"></path></svg></button><div class="flex items-center gap-2"><span class="text-sm">Page</span><input type="text" inputMode="numeric" pattern="[0-9]*" class="w-10 text-center px-1 py-0.5 rounded-none border border-black bg-white text-sm" aria-label="Go to page" value="1"/><span class="text-sm">of <!-- -->1</span></div><button type="button" disabled="" class="disabled:opacity-40" aria-label="Next"><svg width="15" height="15" viewBox="0 0 15 15" fill="none" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" class="w-5 h-5 text-brand-neutral-500 dark:text-brand-neutral-300"><path d="M6.1584 3.13508C6.35985 2.94621 6.67627 2.95642 6.86514 3.15788L10.6151 7.15788C10.7954 7.3502 10.7954 7.64949 10.6151 7.84182L6.86514 11.8418C6.67627 12.0433 6.35985 12.0535 6.1584 11.8646C5.95694 11.6757 5.94673 11.3593 6.1356 11.1579L9.565 7.49985L6.1356 3.84182C5.94673 3.64036 5.95694 3.32394 6.1584 3.13508Z" fill="currentColor" fill-rule="evenodd" clip-rule="evenodd"></path></svg></button></div></div></section><section id="references" aria-label="References" class="scroll-mt-8"><h2 class="text-lg font-[400] mb-3 leading-snug scroll-mt-8">References</h2><ul class="list-none space-y-2 pl-0 text-[13px] leading-snug text-black"><li id="reference-1" class="grid grid-cols-[1.25rem_minmax(0,1fr)] gap-x-1 scroll-mt-8"><span class="tabular-nums">[<!-- -->1<!-- -->]</span><div><div class="leading-snug"><a href="https://arxiv.org/abs/2405.07987" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" class="no-underline hover:underline focus-visible:underline underline-offset-4 decoration-1">Position: The platonic representation hypothesis</a></div><div class="leading-snug">Minyoung Huh, Brian Cheung, Tongzhou Wang, and Phillip Isola<!-- --> · <em>Forty-first International Conference on Machine Learning</em> · <!-- -->2024</div></div></li><li id="reference-2" class="grid grid-cols-[1.25rem_minmax(0,1fr)] gap-x-1 scroll-mt-8"><span class="tabular-nums">[<!-- -->2<!-- -->]</span><div><div class="leading-snug"><a href="https://doi.org/10.1145/3404835.3463257" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" class="no-underline hover:underline focus-visible:underline underline-offset-4 decoration-1">WIT: Wikipedia-based image text dataset for multimodal multilingual machine learning</a></div><div class="leading-snug">Karthik Srinivasan, Ronghang Hu, Ishan Misra, Antoine Miech, Ching-Hua Chaudhuri, Quoc Le, Rahul S